1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:05,079
On the morning of day two, I had a little over one bottle of water and nothing to eat.

2
00:00:05,629 --> 00:00:09,344
The message that came in at dawn said to reach River Crossing before noon.

3
00:00:09,894 --> 00:00:11,784
I didn't know how far that was.

4
00:00:12,134 --> 00:00:15,401
I didn't know if the evacuation point was still operating.

5
00:00:15,751 --> 00:00:19,644
But this room had no water supply, and I couldn't stay here forever.

6
00:00:20,194 --> 00:00:21,561
I decided to go.

7
00:00:22,111 --> 00:00:24,499
I slid the bolt back across the door.

8
00:00:24,849 --> 00:00:27,798
If I was going out, I wanted to do it properly.

9
00:00:28,348 --> 00:00:30,276
I opened the notes on my phone.

10
00:00:30,826 --> 00:00:32,870
Rule one: Noise attracts them.

11
00:00:33,420 --> 00:00:36,419
The water bottle I'd dropped last night had taught me that.

12
00:00:36,969 --> 00:00:40,951
I turned off notification sounds, keyboard sounds, and vibration.

13
00:00:41,301 --> 00:00:43,523
Then I checked for any alarms I'd set.

14
00:00:44,073 --> 00:00:46,512
I didn't want to make the same mistake again.

15
00:00:47,062 --> 00:00:48,531
Next was my hand.

16
00:00:49,081 --> 00:00:51,800
The cloth I'd wrapped around it yesterday was dirty.

17
00:00:52,150 --> 00:00:54,117
One edge had stuck to the scrape.

18
00:00:54,467 --> 00:00:57,186
I peeled it away slowly, but it still hurt.

19
00:00:57,736 --> 00:01:00,366
I replaced it with a cleaner strip of cloth.

20
00:01:00,716 --> 00:01:02,581
I could still move my fingers.

21
00:01:02,931 --> 00:01:04,821
Closing my hand was harder.

22
00:01:05,371 --> 00:01:07,389
I packed the water and flashlight.

23
00:01:07,739 --> 00:01:11,708
Then I checked the zippers and made sure nothing was hanging loose outside the bag.

24
00:01:12,258 --> 00:01:17,107
Before leaving, I took a good look at the door and the buildings around it so I could find my way back.

25
00:01:17,657 --> 00:01:21,703
If I couldn't reach the evacuation point, at least I still had this place.

26
00:01:22,253 --> 00:01:24,654
There were abandoned cars along the street.

27
00:01:25,003 --> 00:01:26,906
Some still had their doors open.

28
00:01:27,256 --> 00:01:29,835
Belongings lay scattered across the pavement.

29
00:01:30,385 --> 00:01:34,801
I stayed near the buildings and avoided gaps between cars where I couldn't see ahead.

30
00:01:35,351 --> 00:01:38,682
At each corner, I stopped to listen before looking around it.

31
00:01:39,232 --> 00:01:42,449
Once, I heard dragging footsteps just beyond a turn.

32
00:01:42,799 --> 00:01:45,302
I waited behind the wall until they passed.

33
00:01:45,852 --> 00:01:49,910
It was slow, but I didn't want to turn a corner and walk straight into one of them.

34
00:01:50,460 --> 00:01:53,792
A sign said River Crossing was eleven kilometers away.

35
00:01:54,342 --> 00:01:55,671
I checked the time.

36
00:01:56,021 --> 00:01:57,477
It wasn't six yet.

37
00:01:58,027 --> 00:02:01,971
With all these stops, I'd be lucky to manage three kilometers an hour.

38
00:02:02,321 --> 00:02:04,326
That meant four or five hours.

39
00:02:04,676 --> 00:02:07,535
If the roads were clear, I could get there before noon.

40
00:02:07,885 --> 00:02:11,714
But I also needed food, and I would have to avoid them along the way.

41
00:02:12,264 --> 00:02:14,435
I put the phone away and kept walking.

42
00:02:14,985 --> 00:02:18,827
On a side street, I spotted one standing beside a parked car.

43
00:02:19,377 --> 00:02:21,713
I crouched behind a delivery truck.

44
00:02:22,063 --> 00:02:25,203
From there, I could watch without stepping out into the open.

45
00:02:25,753 --> 00:02:30,233
It moved slowly between two cars, bumped into a door, then changed direction.

46
00:02:30,783 --> 00:02:32,839
A bird flew off a nearby roof.

47
00:02:33,389 --> 00:02:37,192
It turned toward the sound of the wings, took a few steps, and stopped.

48
00:02:37,742 --> 00:02:38,740
I waited.

49
00:02:39,290 --> 00:02:40,797
There was no more noise.

50
00:02:41,147 --> 00:02:43,713
After a while, it started wandering again.

51
00:02:44,263 --> 00:02:48,028
I still didn't know how well it could see, or whether it could smell me.

52
00:02:48,578 --> 00:02:53,275
All I'd seen was that it reacted to a sound, then stopped following when the sound was gone.

53
00:02:53,825 --> 00:02:56,965
That wasn't enough to assume silence would keep me safe.

54
00:02:57,515 --> 00:03:00,961
I waited until it moved farther away, then crossed the street.

55
00:03:01,511 --> 00:03:05,429
Around seven, I found a convenience store with a broken front window.

56
00:03:05,979 --> 00:03:08,048
I'd been hungry since waking up.

57
00:03:08,598 --> 00:03:11,993
From outside, I could see that most of the shelves were empty.

58
00:03:12,343 --> 00:03:13,953
I still wanted to check.

59
00:03:14,503 --> 00:03:19,059
I listened for a while, then stepped inside, avoiding the larger pieces of glass.

60
00:03:19,609 --> 00:03:21,780
There was a curtain behind the counter.

61
00:03:22,130 --> 00:03:24,785
Before searching for food, I pulled it aside.

62
00:03:25,335 --> 00:03:26,588
A small storeroom.

63
00:03:26,938 --> 00:03:29,147
A fallen shelf blocked the back door.

64
00:03:29,697 --> 00:03:32,658
I wouldn't be able to get out that way if I needed to run.

65
00:03:33,208 --> 00:03:36,425
I went back to the front and only searched near the entrance.

66
00:03:36,975 --> 00:03:38,776
Most of the food was gone.

67
00:03:39,126 --> 00:03:42,036
Empty packets and crushed boxes covered the floor.

68
00:03:42,586 --> 00:03:46,262
Behind the counter, I found an unopened packet of mints and a lighter.

69
00:03:46,812 --> 00:03:47,950
I took both.

70
00:03:48,500 --> 00:03:53,885
I wanted to keep looking, but the longer I stayed, the more chance there was of something reaching the entrance.

71
00:03:54,435 --> 00:03:55,305
I left.

72
00:03:55,855 --> 00:03:57,949
A little sugar was better than nothing.

73
00:03:58,299 --> 00:04:01,363
But a few mints wouldn't be enough for a whole day of walking.

74
00:04:01,913 --> 00:04:05,793
I came to a pedestrian overpass and climbed up to see the roads ahead.

75
00:04:06,343 --> 00:04:08,794
The road toward the river was full of cars.

76
00:04:09,344 --> 00:04:11,744
Some had stopped in the middle of junctions.

77
00:04:12,094 --> 00:04:15,081
Others had driven onto the pavement and been left there.

78
00:04:15,631 --> 00:04:17,573
Figures were moving between them.

79
00:04:18,123 --> 00:04:21,543
I couldn't tell whether they were survivors or more of the infected.

80
00:04:22,093 --> 00:04:23,907
I looked for a quieter route.

81
00:04:24,257 --> 00:04:28,009
If I followed the main road, there would be little room to get around a group.

82
00:04:28,559 --> 00:04:31,904
From the overpass, I spotted a street running alongside it.

83
00:04:32,254 --> 00:04:35,305
There were fewer cars, and it led toward the river too.

84
00:04:35,855 --> 00:04:37,796
I went down and headed that way.

85
00:04:38,346 --> 00:04:40,631
Around nine, I heard a car alarm.

86
00:04:41,181 --> 00:04:44,526
I stopped before the corner and looked from behind a parked bus.

87
00:04:45,076 --> 00:04:47,501
Dozens of them were gathered around the car.

88
00:04:48,051 --> 00:04:50,197
Some were pressed against its doors.

89
00:04:50,547 --> 00:04:52,730
Others were still trying to get closer.

90
00:04:53,280 --> 00:04:55,502
I needed to reach the road beyond them.

91
00:04:56,052 --> 00:04:58,682
Going back to find another route would cost time.

92
00:04:59,032 --> 00:05:01,547
Trying to slip past would bring me too close.

93
00:05:02,097 --> 00:05:04,140
I backed away to the last junction.

94
00:05:04,690 --> 00:05:07,142
The detour wasn't as simple as I'd hoped.

95
00:05:07,492 --> 00:05:09,752
One alley ended at a locked fence.

96
00:05:10,102 --> 00:05:12,579
I had to turn around and try another street.

97
00:05:13,129 --> 00:05:16,090
It took about forty minutes to get past the area.

98
00:05:16,640 --> 00:05:19,066
I stopped in the shade and drank some water.

99
00:05:19,616 --> 00:05:21,328
The bottle was getting low.

100
00:05:21,678 --> 00:05:27,535
I hadn't reached the river yet, and I still needed enough for the walk back if there was nobody at the evacuation point.

101
00:05:28,085 --> 00:05:30,103
I tightened the cap and moved on.

102
00:05:30,653 --> 00:05:32,900
By about ten, my heel was sore.

103
00:05:33,450 --> 00:05:36,513
I stopped in the recessed doorway of a closed pharmacy.

104
00:05:37,063 --> 00:05:40,982
It kept me partly out of sight, but it was still right beside the pavement.

105
00:05:41,532 --> 00:05:45,195
I put the bag between my feet, leaned back, and closed my eyes.

106
00:05:45,745 --> 00:05:47,712
I only meant to rest for a minute.

107
00:05:48,262 --> 00:05:50,509
Dragging footsteps made me open them.

108
00:05:51,059 --> 00:05:54,148
One was coming toward me, about ten meters away.

109
00:05:54,698 --> 00:05:56,142
I pulled my feet in.

110
00:05:56,692 --> 00:05:58,352
My shoe brushed the bag.

111
00:05:58,702 --> 00:05:59,967
I stopped moving.

112
00:06:00,517 --> 00:06:01,783
It kept coming.

113
00:06:02,333 --> 00:06:06,799
I pressed farther into the doorway, trying not to touch the metal shutter behind me.

114
00:06:07,349 --> 00:06:11,165
When it was only a few meters away, my shoulder made the shutter click.

115
00:06:11,715 --> 00:06:12,687
It stopped.

116
00:06:13,237 --> 00:06:14,490
I stayed still.

117
00:06:15,040 --> 00:06:18,448
Then something metal clattered onto the road farther down the street.

118
00:06:18,998 --> 00:06:21,117
It turned toward the noise and moved on.

119
00:06:21,667 --> 00:06:24,871
I waited until I couldn't hear its footsteps before moving.

120
00:06:25,421 --> 00:06:28,370
I didn't know what would have happened without that other sound.

121
00:06:28,920 --> 00:06:31,027
But this wasn't a safe place to sleep.

122
00:06:31,577 --> 00:06:34,564
I stood up, put on the bag, and kept going.

123
00:06:35,114 --> 00:06:37,323
At ten fifty, I saw the river.

124
00:06:37,873 --> 00:06:42,174
Near the bridge, temporary fencing and a concrete wall marked an approach lane.

125
00:06:42,724 --> 00:06:46,706
Inside were traffic cones, an evacuation sign, and a white tent.

126
00:06:47,256 --> 00:06:48,815
I watched from outside.

127
00:06:49,365 --> 00:06:50,566
No staff.

128
00:06:50,916 --> 00:06:52,028
No buses.

129
00:06:52,578 --> 00:06:54,596
The tent blocked part of my view.

130
00:06:54,946 --> 00:06:58,456
I wanted to get closer and check for a notice or anyone inside.

131
00:06:59,006 --> 00:07:04,327
The lane was about a hundred and fifty meters long, with the wall on one side and the fence on the other.

132
00:07:04,877 --> 00:07:07,201
I looked for an opening along the fence.

133
00:07:07,751 --> 00:07:08,953
There wasn't one.

134
00:07:09,503 --> 00:07:12,694
If anything happened, I would have to come back the same way.

135
00:07:13,244 --> 00:07:14,330
I knew that.

136
00:07:14,680 --> 00:07:18,139
But after walking all morning, I didn't want to leave without checking.

137
00:07:18,689 --> 00:07:19,763
I went in.

138
00:07:20,313 --> 00:07:25,239
Under the tent were a folding table, paperwork, and paper cups scattered on the ground.

139
00:07:25,789 --> 00:07:27,182
Nobody was there.

140
00:07:27,732 --> 00:07:30,336
From that point, I could see the bridge clearly.

141
00:07:30,886 --> 00:07:32,713
Cars blocked both lanes.

142
00:07:33,063 --> 00:07:36,279
A large number of infected stood or wandered between them.

143
00:07:36,829 --> 00:07:38,809
There was no queue for transport.

144
00:07:39,159 --> 00:07:40,947
Nobody directing people.

145
00:07:41,497 --> 00:07:42,839
I checked my phone.

146
00:07:43,389 --> 00:07:44,794
Eleven forty-one.

147
00:07:45,344 --> 00:07:48,012
Nineteen minutes before the time in the message.

148
00:07:48,562 --> 00:07:49,968
I thought about leaving.

149
00:07:50,518 --> 00:07:53,505
Then I wondered if the buses simply hadn't arrived yet.

150
00:07:53,855 --> 00:07:56,459
What if I left and they came a few minutes later?

151
00:07:57,009 --> 00:08:00,570
I waited beside the tent, keeping my distance from the bridge.

152
00:08:01,120 --> 00:08:04,490
At noon, the loudspeaker above me suddenly played a chime.

153
00:08:05,040 --> 00:08:07,300
I flinched and stepped away from the pole.

154
00:08:07,850 --> 00:08:09,524
A recorded voice followed.

155
00:08:10,074 --> 00:08:12,359
"Evacuation transport is arriving.

156
00:08:12,709 --> 00:08:15,071
Please proceed to the marked waiting area."

157
00:08:15,621 --> 00:08:17,167
I looked toward the bridge.

158
00:08:17,717 --> 00:08:19,378
No vehicles were moving.

159
00:08:19,928 --> 00:08:22,825
But the nearest infected had turned toward the speaker.

160
00:08:23,375 --> 00:08:25,189
The announcement played again.

161
00:08:25,739 --> 00:08:27,757
They started coming toward the tent.

162
00:08:28,107 --> 00:08:29,767
More followed behind them.

163
00:08:30,317 --> 00:08:32,042
I didn't wait any longer.

164
00:08:32,592 --> 00:08:34,928
I turned and ran back toward the entrance.

165
00:08:35,478 --> 00:08:38,618
There was still a wall on one side and a fence on the other.

166
00:08:38,968 --> 00:08:40,438
Nowhere to turn off.

167
00:08:40,988 --> 00:08:43,350
I had to run the full length of the lane.

168
00:08:43,900 --> 00:08:46,007
Once I was out, I looked back.

169
00:08:46,557 --> 00:08:48,932
The first had almost reached the table.

170
00:08:49,282 --> 00:08:51,631
More were coming off the bridge behind them.

171
00:08:52,181 --> 00:08:55,181
If I'd kept waiting, they would have cut off my way out.

172
00:08:55,731 --> 00:08:58,858
I left the area and turned two corners before stopping.

173
00:08:59,408 --> 00:09:02,765
I crouched behind a dumpster and waited for my breathing to slow.

174
00:09:03,315 --> 00:09:05,142
I could still hear the speaker.

175
00:09:05,692 --> 00:09:08,016
It kept repeating the same announcement.

176
00:09:08,566 --> 00:09:10,405
I took out my phone and wrote:

177
00:09:10,955 --> 00:09:14,159
Rule two: Find another way out before going farther in.

178
00:09:14,709 --> 00:09:17,415
I'd known to check for an exit since yesterday.

179
00:09:17,965 --> 00:09:20,646
I'd even checked the back door in the store that morning.

180
00:09:21,196 --> 00:09:24,260
But at the evacuation point, I'd ignored the problem.

181
00:09:24,810 --> 00:09:28,205
I'd seen the sign and the tent and hoped there were people who could help.

182
00:09:28,555 --> 00:09:31,797
I'd kept going even though I knew there was only one way back.

183
00:09:32,347 --> 00:09:37,146
I didn't know whether the message was old or the evacuation point had only just been abandoned.

184
00:09:37,696 --> 00:09:39,433
Knowing wouldn't help me now.

185
00:09:39,983 --> 00:09:43,123
I needed to leave before the speaker attracted more of them.

186
00:09:43,673 --> 00:09:46,188
I considered looking for somewhere nearby.

187
00:09:46,738 --> 00:09:48,539
But I didn't know the area.

188
00:09:48,889 --> 00:09:50,983
I had no food and little water.

189
00:09:51,533 --> 00:09:53,985
At least the old room had a door I could lock.

190
00:09:54,335 --> 00:09:56,582
I decided to get back before dark.

191
00:09:57,132 --> 00:09:58,780
The return was slower.

192
00:09:59,330 --> 00:10:01,182
I'd been walking since morning.

193
00:10:01,532 --> 00:10:04,276
My feet hurt, and I'd eaten only a few mints.

194
00:10:04,826 --> 00:10:09,013
Where I wasn't sure of the route, I stopped to check street signs and look for landmarks.

195
00:10:09,563 --> 00:10:13,022
Near a bus stop, I stepped off the curb without looking down.

196
00:10:13,572 --> 00:10:16,686
A loose piece of broken concrete shifted under my shoe.

197
00:10:17,036 --> 00:10:18,314
My ankle rolled.

198
00:10:18,864 --> 00:10:21,443
I grabbed the bus shelter to keep from falling.

199
00:10:21,993 --> 00:10:24,687
It hurt enough that I had to stand still for a while.

200
00:10:25,237 --> 00:10:26,987
I tried putting my foot down.

201
00:10:27,337 --> 00:10:29,903
It could take some weight, but every step hurt.

202
00:10:30,453 --> 00:10:32,688
I didn't know anywhere closer to go.

203
00:10:33,238 --> 00:10:36,977
I carried on, moving more slowly and stopping to rest several times.

204
00:10:37,527 --> 00:10:40,553
By then, I just wanted to reach the room before dark.

205
00:10:41,103 --> 00:10:43,949
It was late afternoon when I reached the row of shops.

206
00:10:44,499 --> 00:10:46,517
The steel door was still closed.

207
00:10:47,067 --> 00:10:50,143
I listened outside and checked around me before opening it.

208
00:10:50,693 --> 00:10:53,936
Inside, I slid the bolt across and sat on the floor.

209
00:10:54,486 --> 00:10:57,511
I'd walked all day and ended up back where I'd started.

210
00:10:58,061 --> 00:11:01,035
All I'd brought back was a lighter and the remaining mints.

211
00:11:01,585 --> 00:11:04,164
There were only a few mouthfuls of water left.

212
00:11:04,714 --> 00:11:06,158
I took off my shoe.

213
00:11:06,508 --> 00:11:08,041
My ankle was swollen.

214
00:11:08,591 --> 00:11:10,928
My hand hurt more than it had that morning.

215
00:11:11,278 --> 00:11:14,966
The scrape had opened again while I was running and grabbing onto things.

216
00:11:15,516 --> 00:11:18,108
I changed the cloth around it and checked my phone.

217
00:11:18,658 --> 00:11:21,211
There was still battery, but no new message.

218
00:11:21,761 --> 00:11:23,243
I looked at the water.

219
00:11:23,793 --> 00:11:25,390
Not enough for tomorrow.

220
00:11:25,940 --> 00:11:28,902
I'd gone to the evacuation point expecting help.

221
00:11:29,252 --> 00:11:33,565
Now I still needed to find water and food, and walking was harder than before.

222
00:11:34,115 --> 00:11:36,222
Tomorrow, I had to find water.

223
00:11:36,772 --> 00:11:39,058
I couldn't afford another day like this.
